-- title:
--   Corollary 3.2 (corrected) — $E_{f,n}\mathscr B_{r,n}E_{f,n} = \mathscr B_{r,n-2f}E_{f,n}$
-- statement:
--   Let $F$, $r \ge 1$, $q$, $u$, $\varepsilon$ be as in the setting, and let $f$ be a positive integer with $f \le \lfloor n/2 \rfloor$. Assume either $2f<n$ or $\omega_a\ne0$ for some integer $a$. With $E_{f,n} = E_{n-1}E_{n-3}\cdots E_{n-2f+1}$ and $\mathscr B_{r,n-2f} \subseteq \mathscr B_{r,n}$ the subalgebra generated by $T_i, E_i$ ($i < n-2f$) and $X_j^{\pm 1}$ ($j \le n-2f$),
--   $$E_{f,n}\,\mathscr B_{r,n}\,E_{f,n} = \mathscr B_{r,n-2f}\,E_{f,n}.$$
--
--   This iterates the corrected Lemma 3.1. The condition on $\omega$ addresses the final two-strand corner when $n=2f$; the paper's unconditional statement includes a false $n=2$, $f=1$ case.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Both sides are sets of elements of $\mathscr B_{r,n}$; on the right the subalgebra element stands to the left of $E_{f,n}$, as printed. In 0-based indices $E_{f,n}$ is the ordered product of the generators with indices $n-2, n-4, \dots, n-2f$.
-- source:
--   Rui and Si, The representation theory of cyclotomic BMW algebras, arXiv:0807.4149v1, p. 7, Corollary 3.2

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CycBMW_Semisimple_Setting

namespace CycBMW.Semisimple

/-- Corrected Corollary 3.2, p. 7. The final two-strand corner in the printed
iteration requires a nonzero unwrapping parameter when `n = 2f`. -/
theorem corollary_3_2 {F : Type*} [Field F] (r n : ℕ) (hr : 1 ≤ r)
    (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) (ε : ℤˣ) (hq : q ≠ 0) (hq2 : q ^ 2 ≠ 1)
    (hu : ∀ i, u i ≠ 0) (hinj : Function.Injective u)
    (f : ℕ) (hf : 1 ≤ f) (hfn : f ≤ n / 2)
    (hcorner : 2 * f < n ∨ ∃ a : ℤ, omega r q u ε a ≠ 0) :
    {x : B F r n q u ε | ∃ b : B F r n q u ε,
        x = Efn F r n q u ε f * b * Efn F r n q u ε f} =
      {x : B F r n q u ε | ∃ b ∈ Bsub F r n q u ε (n - 2 * f),
        x = b * Efn F r n q u ε f} := by sorry

end CycBMW.Semisimple
